{
  "title": "Namaz of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)",
  "data": "Pray 2 units. In each unit, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Qadr](A101) 15 times.\nRecite [Surah al-Qadr](A101) 15 times more at each of these points: in ruku', after rising from ruku', in the first sajdah, after rising from it, in the second sajdah, and after rising from it.\nAfter the prayer, recite:\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ رَبُّنَا وَرَبُّ اٰبَاۤئِنَا الْاَوَّلِيْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU RABBUNAA WA RABBU AABAA'INAL AWWALEEN\nThere is no god save Allah; our Lord and the Lord of our fathers of old.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ اِلٰهًا وَاحِدًا وَنَحْنُ لَهٗ مُسْلِمُوْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU ILAAHAN WAAHIDAN WA NAHNU LAHOO MUSLIMOON\nThere is no god save Allah; one God, and to Him are we submissive.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ لَا نَعْبُدُ اِلَّاۤ اِيَّاهُ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ وَلَوْ كَرِهَ الْمُشْرِكُوْنَ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU LAA NA'BUDU ILLAA IYYAAHU MUKHLISEENA LAHUD DEENA WA LAW KARIHAL MUSHRIKOON\nThere is no god save Allah; we worship none save Him, making our devotion sincere as in His sight even though the polytheists may detest it.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَحْدَهٗ وَحْدَهٗ وَحْدَهٗ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO WAHDAHOO WAHDAH\nThere is no god save Allah; alone, alone, alone.\nاَنْجَزَ وَعْدَهٗ وَنَصَرَ عَبْدَهٗ وَاَعَزَّ جُنْدَهٗ وَهَزَمَ الْاَحْزَابَ وَحْدَهٗ\nANJAZA WA'DAHOO WA NASARA A'BDAHOO WA A'AZZA JUNDAHOO WA HAZAMAL AHZAABA WAHDAH\nHe has truly fulfilled His promise, granted His servant victory, made powerful His soldiers, and defeated the parties alone.\nفَلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nFALAHUL MULKU WA LAHUL HAMDU WA HUWA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nAll sovereignty be His and all praise be to Him. And He has power over all things.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَنْتَ نُوْرُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّ فَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ [وَلِلّٰهِ الْمُلْكُ وَالْحَمْدُ]\nALLAAHUMMA ANTA NOORUS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDI WA MAN FEEHINNA FALAKAL HAMDU (WA LILLAAHIL MULKU WAL HAMD)\nO Allah, You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and whatever is in these two. So, all praise be to You. [And to Allah belong all sovereignty and praise.]\nوَاَنْتَ قَيَّامُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّ فَلَكَ الْحَمْدُ\nWA ANTA QAYYAAMUS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARDI WA MAN FEEHINNA FALAKAL HAMD\nAnd You are the Fashioner of the heavens and the earth and whatever exists in these two. So, all praise be to You.\nوَاَنْتَ الْحَقُّ وَوَعْدُكَ الْحَقُّ [حَقٌّ]، وَقَوْلُكَ حَقٌّ وَاِنْجَازُكَ حَقٌّ\nWA ANTAL HAQQU WA WA'DUKAL HAQQU (HAQQUN) WA QAWLUKA HAQQUN WA INJAAZUKA HAQQ\nYou are the (utter) Truth, Your promise is utterly true, Your word is true, Your fulfillment is true,\nوَالْجَنَّةُ حَقٌّ وَالنَّارُ حَقٌّ [وَاَنْتَ الْحَقُّ]\nWAL JANNATU HAQQUN WAN NAARU HAQQUN (WA ANTAL HAQQ)\nParadise is true, and Hellfire is true. [And You are the Truth.]\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَكَ اَسْلَمْتُ وَبِكَ اٰمَنْتُ وَعَلَيْكَ تَوَكَّلْتُ\nALLAAHUMMA LAKA ASLAMTU WA BIKA AAMANTU WA A'LAYKA TAWAKKALT\nO Allah, to You have I surrendered, in You do I believe, on You do I rely,\nوَبِكَ خَاصَمْتُ وَاِلَيْكَ حَاكَمْتُ\nWA BIKA KHAASAMTU WA ILAYKA HAAKAMT\nfor Your sake do I dispute, and Your Judgement do I seek.\nيَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ يَا رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِيْ مَا قَدَّمْتُ وَاَخَّرْتُ وَاَسْرَرْتُ وَاَعْلَنْتُ\nYAA RABBI YAA RABBI YAA RABBIGH FIR LEE MAA QADDAMTU WA AKHKHARTU WA ASRARTU WA A'LANT\nO my Lord; O my Lord; O my Lord; (please) forgive me my past and next sins and my hidden and open ones.\nاَنْتَ اِلٰهِيْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ\nANTA ILAAHEE LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANT\nYou are verily my God; there is no god save You.\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاغْفِرْ لِيْ وَارْحَمْنِي وَتُبْ عَلَيَّ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WAGHFIR LEE WARHAMNEE WA TUB A'LAYY\nSend blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, forgive me, have mercy on me, and accept my repentance.\nاِنَّكَ اَنْتَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيْمُ.\nINNAKA ANTAT TAWWAABUR RAHEEM\nVerily, You are the Oft-Returning, the Most Merciful.",
  "merits": "Sayyid Ibn Tawus, may Allah have mercy on him, has narrated, through an authenticated chain of authority, that when he was asked about Ja'far al-Tayyar's Prayer, Imam al-Rida (a.s.) said, \"Have you known about the Holy Prophet's Prayer? Perhaps, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) had never offered Ja'far al-Tayyar's Prayer and Ja'far al-Tayyar had never offered the Holy Prophet's Prayer.\" When the asker asked him to teach him that prayer, Imam al-Rida (a.s.) described it.\n\nHe said: When you finish your prayer, you will have all your sins forgiven by Almighty Allah and you will have all your requests granted for you."
}
